<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mughan plain</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mughan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mughan plain is a lowland steppe south of the Aras river, divided today between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. It was a traditional pasture and gathering place for armies and tribes. In 1736 it was the site of the assembly at which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> was proclaimed ruler, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a> and founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mughan-plain.jpg" alt="Mughan plain" width="301" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vasilii Pyadyshev · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mughan_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
